WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
Why do we sometimes fail to perform 
up to our&nbsp;potential under pressure?

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.002
We often get in our own way

00:00:07.002 --> 00:00:12.342
precisely because our worries 
prompt&nbsp;us to concentrate too much.

00:00:12.342 --> 00:00:15.806
So what do we do? A lot of it comes 
down to the prefrontal&nbsp;cortex,

00:00:15.806 --> 00:00:18.934
that front part of our brain 
that sits over our eyes

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:22.000
and usually helps us focus&nbsp;in positive ways.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.669
It often gets hooked on the wrong things.

00:00:24.669 --> 00:00:26.444
So how do we unhook it?

00:00:26.444 --> 00:00:28.858
Something as simple as singing a song,

00:00:28.858 --> 00:00:33.129
can help us take our mind 
off those pesky details.

00:00:33.129 --> 00:00:38.142
It's also true that practicing under conditions 
that we're going to perform under --

00:00:38.142 --> 00:00:41.049
closing&nbsp;the gap between 
training and competition

00:00:41.049 --> 00:00:44.631
can help us get used to 
that feeling of all eyes on&nbsp;us.

00:00:44.631 --> 00:00:47.257
When you're taking a test, close the book,

00:00:47.257 --> 00:00:51.209
practice retrieving the answer from 
memory&nbsp;under timed situations.

00:00:51.209 --> 00:00:54.464
The ability to get used to 
what it will feel like

00:00:54.464 --> 00:00:58.141
can make the&nbsp;difference in 
whether we choke or thrive.

